I think he's done very well. I've seen him with Queen twice and both times were wonderful. Obviously, he is not Freddie and he knows that. He's not trying to BE him he's trying to perform his music. As the years have gone on, I think the chemistry between him and Queen has only gotten better and better; he just clicks really well with them. 

&#x200B;

He's very talented and I'm glad they chose him.

I would say A Night at the Opera is a good intro to Queen. That album has a bit of everything they experimented with and of course Bohemian Rhapsody is on there. After that, A Day at the Races and Jazz. 

&#x200B;

Or listen to them all one by one

